  "notes": "Modified cash basis city, FY ended 9/30/2023. Governmental lines from the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures, and Changes in Fund Balances - Governmental Funds (pp8-9), Total Governmental Funds column; transfers in 570,561 is the Total column after the Eliminations column (General out 325,183 to Debt Service eliminated). Fund balances are recorded as fund balances (beginning 9,011,016, ending 8,170,804, p9); beginning cash not printed; ending_cash = sum of the four cash lines of the governmental funds statement of assets (p5). Business-type lines from the modified cash proprietary Statement of Revenues, Expenses, and Changes in Net Position (p11), which ties to the Statement of Activities business-type column (pp3-4) except for 2 dollars of rounding; measure net position (modified cash net position includes capital assets). Proprietary 'Other' 258,747 is charges for services because the Statement of Activities counts it in Charges for Services. Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position - Modified Cash Basis (pp1-2), since the governmental funds statement (8,170,804) does not equal the government-wide governmental figures (capital assets, debt). Detail: the only supplementary schedule is the all-funds budgetary-basis comparison (p14), so detail is per fund column of the governmental funds statement (General, Debt Service, Community Redevelopment) and the single proprietary fund statement; p14 lines not recorded. Pages 15-16 are a second proprietary statement of revenues/expenses and cash flows (report pp53-54, supplementary, no basis in the title) with different figures (charges for services 12,422,177, net position beginning 21,286,551 / ending 22,894,795); not used, since the modified cash statement p11 ties to the Statement of Activities. Proprietary cash flow statements not recorded (cash basis report; proprietary = null). Read pages 1-16 of 16"
}
